# Plain HTTP on Caddy's port 80, which the local stack publishes on the host's
# 8020. The host matcher ignores the port, so requests to localhost:8020 land
# here.
#
# The prerenderer resolves `localhost` to its own container, so the site also
# answers to its compose service name, and that name is the render origin.

http://localhost, http://tt-caddy {
    import base.Caddyfile http://tt-caddy

    # The mail stub's page, on the site's origin, so the relative links in the
    # emails it shows open the site.
    handle /mail {
        reverse_proxy tt-mail:3000
    }
}
